FIXED: The disjoint expression consolidation (DEC) transformation created non-exhaustive case-expressions when the consolidated function was not applied in every alternative. When constant propagation later reduced such a case-expression, compilation failed with `Clash error call: scrutinise: ...`. The argument-selecting case-expressions now carry a default alternative for the branches in which the consolidated function is not used [#2770](https://github.com/clash-lang/clash-compiler/issues/2770).
